      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Every primitive the app treats as first-class has one spec graph in the primitive library, written the same way, checked against the code, and listed in one index",
        "body": "**Status, 2026-09-24:** three specs exist and are in progress (Declaration, Surface, Bridge). Eleven are not started. Four of those are additions the authoritative list does not name; question 2 asks you to confirm them.\n\n**Where the list comes from.** The authoritative list is the table in `AGENTS.md`: `declaration`, `view`, `content`, `glyph`, `field`, `port`, `portal`, `script`, `bridge` (script and bridge marked advanced). The library that should hold one graph per primitive is `primitives/` in `mikemartinez1974/public`; its index (`primitives/root.node`) lists three portals: Declaration, Bridge and Surface. Surface is not a node type, so it does not count toward the nine.\n\n**Three lists disagree with it, and this graph replaces the guesswork:**\n- `topics/twilite-graph-primitives` is a topic graph with concepts for Declaration, Port, View, Content, Glyph, Portal and Bridge. It has no Field or Script.\n- `docs/primitive-direction-2026-05.md` is out of date: it lists `markdown` as a core primitive (it became `content`) and has no glyph or portal.\n- The node type registry (`components/GraphEditor/nodeTypeRegistry.js`) holds many more types than nine. Most are legacy or utility types, and question 6 asks how to say so.\n\n**What \"done\" means for a primitive.** One graph at `primitives/<name>/root.node` with the eight sections the three existing specs use: Meaning, Invariants, Contract, Ports and Relationships, Behavior, Representations, Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive, Examples. It says what is real in the app today versus proposed, cites the real files, follows the canonical spatial layout, validates cleanly, is linked from the index, and has a test. Task 1 writes that form down once.\n\n**Recommended order, by what depends on what:** content, view, glyph, port, portal, field, edge, event handler, method, script, membrane. Content and View come first because every other spec points at them.\n\n**Decisions the owner has not made yet are in the open questions. Nothing here is built except the three specs marked in progress.**",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "primitives/root.node lists every primitive, with a portal to its spec, and says which are advanced and which are concepts rather than node types",
          "Each spec exists, has the eight sections, and states what is real in the app versus proposed",
          "No spec contradicts the code, AGENTS.md, or another spec (checked against the Declaration and Surface specs, which were reconciled on 2026-09-24)",
          "A test walks primitives/ and fails when a spec is invalid, mis-laid-out, missing a section, or unlisted",
          "The stale lists (the topic graph and docs/primitive-direction-2026-05.md) are corrected or retired"
        ],
