      "data": {
        "title": "1. Write down the form of a primitive spec",
        "body": "Three specs exist, and they share a form that nobody has written down. Write it once, so the other eleven are consistent.\n\nThe eight sections: **Meaning** (what is this thing), **Invariants** (what makes it this and not something else), **Contract** (what data belongs to it), **Ports and Relationships**, **Behavior** (real today versus proposed), **Representations**, **Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive**, **Examples** (referenced by portal, never embedded).\n\nAlso fix the practice: cite real files and functions; never describe a field the code does not read; say when something is a guess; lay the graph out by the canonical layout (Declaration top left, the section nodes in the interior); validate with `validateGraphInvariants`; and link examples with a portal.\n\nPut it where a writer will find it: a short spec graph or a section of the index, and one line in `AGENTS.md`.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The form is written in one place and linked from primitives/root.node",
          "The three existing specs are checked against it and any gap is listed",
          "AGENTS.md points to it"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
