      "data": {
        "title": "2. Declaration",
        "body": "The graph handshake and implicit root. Identity, intent, a Surface port, a landing surface, optional Ports, authority, settings, address.\n\nContract lives in `components/GraphEditor/utils/declarationRelationshipHandles.js`, `systemNodeDefaults.js` (`createDefaultDeclarationNode`, `createDefaultGraph`), `validators/validateGraphInvariants.js`, and the contract docs (`graph-native-node-composition.md`, `twilite-structural-model-inventory.md`).\n\nKeep in step with: `tasks/declaration-surfaces` (the code work that makes the spec true) and `templates/declaration-template` (the draft template, class and worked example).\n\n**Built so far:** `primitives/declaration/root.node` exists with all eight sections. 2026-09-24: `dependencies.nodeTypes` removed from the Contract; Ports rewritten around one repeatable `surface` relationship (the five older relationships marked legacy); Representations says the card comes from a template; the Behavior section removed as superseded; Examples now links the Weekend Reading Group through a portal. Remaining: the Status paragraph in Ports goes stale as `tasks/declaration-surfaces` tasks 7, 8, 11 and 12 land, and the Declaration template is still a draft.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The Status paragraph names only what is shipped",
          "Every \"not yet\" item is tracked in tasks/declaration-surfaces",
          "The Examples node links a real graph"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
