      "data": {
        "title": "3. Surface",
        "body": "A named presentation track: a chain of Views ending in a Glyph. Not a node type: it is drawn as edges (a `surface` edge carrying `data.surfaceId`, then `view-sequence` edges).\n\nContract lives in `components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js` (`collectSurfaceChains`, `resolveSurface`, `resolveSurfaceGlyph`), `graphViewPresentation.js` (the ladder), `viewResolution.js`, and the edge classes in `classes/edges/surface` and `view-sequence`.\n\nQuestion 1 asks whether Surface belongs in the library index next to the node types or under a \"concepts\" heading.\n\n**Built so far:** `primitives/surface/root.node` exists with all eight sections. 2026-09-24: reconciled with what shipped (Surface identity is the edge, Views carry no `surfaceId`, a host may say what it can render, legacy graphs read as one default Surface, what is and is not built). Remaining: it has no linked example (the Weekend Reading Group draws one Surface and could be it), and the host section waits on `tasks/declaration-surfaces` task 11.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The index says Surface is a concept, not a node type",
          "The web and 3D hosts are described as they are (host tag in the payload name; 3D not built)",
          "The Examples node links a graph that draws a Surface"
        ],
