      "data": {
        "title": "6. View",
        "body": "A renderable surface. Its role comes from its place in a Surface's chain (or a Port's relationship), not from a level field. May own `data.content` or delegate.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/ViewNode.js`, `DynamicViewNode.js` (rendering), `createDefaultViewNode`, `utils/viewResolution.js` (`authoredViewResolution`, `semanticZoom.resolution`), `viewSequence.js`, `surfaceChains.js`, `viewExposure.js`, and `tests/viewOwnContentPortal.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: the payload name carries the host (`node.web.detail`, `editor.web`); a View may have `sequence-in` and `sequence-out` ports and a `surface-delegate` port; resolution is continuous and unbounded, not three bands.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States how a View is resolved by resolution and by name",
          "Lists its ports (root, surface-delegate, sequence-in, sequence-out)",
          "Says what the payload name encodes"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
