      "data": {
        "title": "7. Glyph",
        "body": "Symbolic identity, and the end of every Surface's chain. `data.glyph = { kind, name }`, for example an icon name. Not an icon View.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/GlyphNode.js`, `utils/glyphDefinition.js`, `glyphCatalog.js`, `components/TypeGlyph.js`, `createDefaultGlyphNode`, `surfaceChains.js` (`resolveSurfaceGlyph`), and `tests/glyphDefinition.test.js`, `hitboxGlyph.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: older graphs store a glyph as a bare string (the Page Template's is `\"▤\"`) and the Declaration can carry `data.glyph` directly. Say which forms are read.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the glyph definition shapes the app reads",
          "Says a Glyph ends a Surface and takes sequence-in only",
          "Distinguishes it from an icon View"
