      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "8. Port",
        "body": "A named connection endpoint at a node boundary. Its label is its public name. Points to Views; stores none inline.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/PortNode.js`, `utils/portRelationshipHandles.js` (`PORT_SEMANTIC_RELATIONSHIPS`), `portDeclarations.js`, `portEndpoint.js`, `graphNodeContract.js` (`resolveGraphPortPresentation`), and `tests/portDeclarations.test.js`, `dynamicPortDeclarations.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: Ports keep the default, summary, icon and glyph relationships, while the Declaration moved to the Surface relationship (decided 2026-09-24). The spec must say so, and that the Declaration is the implicit root Port.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the Port relationships and why they differ from the Declaration",
          "Says a Declaration is the implicit root Port",
          "Explains handles versus ports"
        ],
