      "data": {
        "title": "11. Edge and Edge Class",
        "body": "RECOMMENDED ADDITION (question 2). An edge connects two Ports; an Edge Class is the graph that states its connection rule.\n\nContract lives in `utils/edgeLegality.js` (`sourceKinds`, `targetKinds`, `maxOutgoing`, `maxIncoming`), `edgeClass.js`, `edgeClassRegistry.js`, the core classes in `mikemartinez1974/public/classes/edges/` (surface, view-sequence, default-view, shared-summary, shared-icon, shared-glyph, landing-surface, invokes), `tests/edgeLegality.test.js`, `coreEdgeClasses.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: legality is a warning on load and an error when mutating (this bit the Declaration template); the classes are fetched from GitHub at startup, so a rule change needs a publish; cross-graph edges are stored on both Declarations.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the rule fields and where each is checked",
          "Lists the core classes and what each connects",
          "Says load versus mutate behavior and when classes are read"
        ],
