      "data": {
        "title": "15. Membrane (Boundary)",
        "body": "RECOMMENDED ADDITION (question 2). A hand-authored chain of control-point nodes that gives a graph a custom boundary shape, instead of the rectangle its landing surface implies.\n\nContract lives in the `membrane` entry of `nodeTypeRegistry.js`, `createDefaultMembraneNode`, `components/NodeGraph/membraneGeometry.js`, `components/NodeGraph/membraneChain.js`, the Declaration's `boundary-begin` and `boundary-end` relationships, the `MEMBRANE_CHAIN_INCOMPLETE` validation, and `tests/membraneGeometry.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: the authored interface frame and how the membrane relates to it; a chain must be complete and unbranched.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the chain rule (complete, unbranched, closed)",
          "Says how the shape relates to the authored frame",
          "Names the validator code"
        ],
