      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "16. The index and the stale lists",
        "body": "Make the index true and retire the wrong lists.\n\n`primitives/root.node` lists three portals and says nothing about what is missing. It should list every primitive with a portal, mark advanced ones, and put concepts (Surface) under their own heading. Then fix or retire `topics/twilite-graph-primitives` (add Field and Script, or say it is a different kind of document), `docs/primitive-direction-2026-05.md` (mark superseded: it names `markdown` as core), and check `OnboardLLM.md` and `AGENTS.md` for the same drift.\n\nDo this LAST, and only list a primitive once its spec exists, so the index never promises a page that is not there.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The index matches the specs that exist",
          "The stale lists are corrected or marked superseded",
          "AGENTS.md, OnboardLLM.md and the index name the same set"
        ],
