      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "17. A test that keeps every spec honest",
        "body": "Add one test file that walks `primitives/` in the public library (skipped when it is not next to this repo, as `tests/declarationTemplate.test.js` is) and checks each spec: valid in load and mutate modes with the edge classes loaded; the eight sections present; laid out by the canonical layout with no overlaps; every portal in it names a graph that exists; and every spec is listed in the index and every index entry has a spec.\n\nThe Declaration Template, the Custom Declaration class and the example already have tests written this way; copy their helpers.\n\nAlso decide whether the specs publish to the twilite-zone repo (question 5), because the test and the links assume where they live.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A failing spec fails the suite",
          "An unlisted or missing spec fails the suite",
          "The test skips cleanly when the public library is absent"
        ],
