      "data": {
        "title": "1. Is Surface a primitive, or a concept that lives beside them?",
        "body": "Surface has a spec graph and is listed in the library index, but it is not a node type: it is drawn as `surface` and `view-sequence` edges. Recommendation: keep its spec, but give the index two headings, \"Primitives\" (things that are nodes) and \"Concepts\" (things built from them, such as Surface), so the count of nine stays honest. Say if you would rather it sit under Declaration or View.",
