      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "2. Are Edge, Event Handler, Method and Membrane primitives?",
        "body": "The authoritative table names nine. These four are first-class in the code: each is a node type or a core class with a contract and tests, and the structural model and AGENTS.md give them rules. I have listed them as recommended additions (tasks 11 to 13 and 15).\n\nRecommendation: yes for Edge (its rule is the only place connection legality is written), Event Handler and Method (both node types with contracts), and Membrane (a registered node type with its own validation). Say which to drop. If you agree, the AGENTS.md table should gain them.",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "open-question",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
