      "data": {
        "title": "3. Are Property, Node Class, Template, Collection, Workspace and Minimap primitives?",
        "body": "They are real, and the app has code for each, but each is built from the primitives rather than being one: a Node Class, a Template and a Collection are graphs whose Declaration names them (`intent.kind`); a Property is a class-backed node; a Workspace is a composition of graphs; the Minimap is a view of one. Recommendation: not primitives. Give them \"patterns\" specs later, after the primitives exist, and mention them in the index so nobody wonders where they are.",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "open-question",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
