      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "6. What do we say about the legacy and utility node types?",
        "body": "The registry holds many types that are not on the list: `markdown`, `svg`, `dictionary`, `legend`, `manifest` (an older Declaration), `subscription`, `div`, `embed`, `canvas`, `target`, and the utility nodes (`timer`, `toggle`, `counter`, `gate`, `delay`, `api`). Recommendation: one short \"Not primitives\" node in the index, naming each as legacy (readable, not for new graphs) or utility, so nobody adds one to the list by accident. I have not read each type's use; that node needs a check of the code first.",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "prominence": "high",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "open-question",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
